prx0r/datagarden =E2=80=94 Complete Peer Review & Dev Instructions

Reviewed: prx0r/datagarden
Head reviewed: 61364930 (=E2=80=9CMuse connector docs: how to connect UKGra=
ph to
Muse=E2=80=9D, 2026-09-19)
Purpose of review: assess the repo against the current UKGraph/Data Garden
thesis and turn the result into concrete development instructions.
EXECUTIVE VERDICT

Do NOT restart the repo.

The thesis is now strong and the repo contains enough useful kernel to
preserve:

   - canonical observations/provenance
   - Route
   - CapabilityEnvelope
   - DecisionSpec
   - Receipt / Actuality
   - source registry
   - normalization pipeline
   - collectors
   - UKBoring proof-of-concept
   - MCP implementations
   - content/experiment machinery

However, the current implementation still mixes three generations of
architecture:

   1. old =E2=80=9Cfour forests / many MCP tools=E2=80=9D architecture,
   2. UKBoring workflow architecture,
   3. new UKGraph economic-router architecture.

The result is conceptual duplication, duplicated models/storage, stale
docs, and=E2=80=94more seriously=E2=80=94several places where demo assumpti=
ons are
presented as economic truth.

The next phase should be a CONVERGENCE + ONE-END-TO-END-ROUTE phase.

Do not add more gardens until that is complete.

The north-star remains:

PERSON + GOAL
=C3=97 CURRENT UK REALITY
=C3=97 HISTORICAL UK REALITY
=E2=86=92 ACTIONABLE ROUTE
=E2=86=92 AGENT ACTION
=E2=86=92 EXTERNAL EVIDENCE
=E2=86=92 VERIFIED OUTCOME
=E2=86=92 BETTER ROUTING

The repo is successful when ChatGPT/Muse with UKGraph can answer:

=E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99m in Oldham, I=E2=80=99m an electrician, I have Saturday=
 free and =C2=A3500. What can
I do to make money?=E2=80=9D

with 2=E2=80=933 genuinely current, evidenced, executable routes that are
materially better than ordinary web search.
WHAT IS STRONG 1. SPEC.md is now the correct source-of-truth direction

The current SPEC captures the important invariants:

   - Data Garden =3D unique transformation =C3=97 continuous collection =C3=
=97 time
   - irreversible-time test
   - one outward UKGraph connector
   - many internal gardens
   - CapabilityEnvelope
   - Route
   - Jev as semantic compiler
   - QP-lite as truth boundary
   - UKBoring / UKOpportunity / UKProducts separation
   - attention truth !=3D economic truth
   - hypothesis / kill conditions
   - verified outcomes as moat

This is the right conceptual base.

KEEP SPEC.md.
2. core/route.py is directionally correct

The Route object already contains most of the fields the final system needs=
:

   - route_type
   - expected value
   - time/capital
   - capabilities
   - constraints
   - why_now / why_person
   - evidence
   - execution type
   - success proof
   - freshness
   - transformation lineage

This should become the canonical outbound object.
3. core/capability_envelope.py is the correct privacy boundary

Good principle:

   - Muse/ChatGPT keeps the user=E2=80=99s deep personal context.
   - UKGraph receives only a task-specific capability envelope.

Keep this.
4. core/observation.py has the right epistemic vocabulary

TruthClass and Recoverability are useful:

   - VERIFIED
   - DERIVED
   - ESTIMATED
   - HEURISTIC
   - CONCEPTUAL
   - UNAVAILABLE

and:

   - canonical
   - third-party
   - partial
   - ephemeral

This maps directly onto Data Garden economics.
5. core/decision_spec.py is the right Jev abstraction

Versioned semantic decisions with:

   - primitive
   - question
   - outputs
   - consequence
   - confidence threshold
   - fallback
   - eval set
   - calibration

This is exactly how Jev should be used.

The problem is not the model; the problem is that the live earn path barely
uses it yet.
6. UKBoring receipt thinking is strategically valuable

The repo has correctly discovered the important distinction:

CLICKED SUBMIT
!=3D
SUBMISSION ACKNOWLEDGED
!=3D
APPLICATION ACCEPTED
!=3D
OUTCOME COMPLETED

This is worth preserving.
7. There is now real collection infrastructure

Planning, Contracts Finder, ONS/ASHE, product/history work, and daily
collection exist.

This is no longer only a document repo.
P0 =E2=80=94 CRITICAL PROBLEMS TO FIX BEFORE EXPOSING UKGRAPH TO AN AGENT P=
0.1 =E2=80=94
uk.earn() currently recommends awarded contracts as bid opportunities

File:

   - collectors/contracts_collector.py
   - uk_boring/earn.py

The collector explicitly requests:

   - type =3D Contract
   - status =3D Awarded

It stores:

   - awardedValue
   - awardedSupplier
   - awardedDate

But _find_contracts() turns those historical awards into:

action =3D BID_CONTRACT

and estimates:
expected_value =3D contract value =C3=97 0.1

This is semantically wrong.

The evidence even says:
=E2=80=9CAwarded to {supplier} for =C2=A3X=E2=80=9D

while the route says:
=E2=80=9CBID_CONTRACT=E2=80=9D

That is exactly the kind of failure UKGraph must never produce.

FIX:
Split procurement into distinct semantic objects:

   1.

   PROCUREMENT_OPPORTUNITY
   - live
      - future / open
      - deadline
      - eligibility
      - action =3D BID / EXPRESS_INTEREST
   2.

   PROCUREMENT_AWARD
   - historical
      - supplier
      - value
      - date
      - useful for market intelligence / win-history / buyer behavior

Awards can help derive:

   - what buyers purchase
   - incumbent suppliers
   - typical values
   - SME accessibility hypotheses

They cannot be emitted as current bid routes.

ACCEPTANCE TEST:
No route with action=3DBID_CONTRACT may derive only from an Awarded notice.
P0.2 =E2=80=94 the planning collector does not collect =E2=80=9Crecent=E2=
=80=9D or =E2=80=9COldham=E2=80=9D

File:

   - collectors/planning_collector.py

collect_recent_applications(days=3D30, limit=3D100):

   - accepts days
   - DOES NOT use days in the API query
   - does not filter locality
   - fetches the first entity results returned by planning.data.gov.uk

The canonical sample confirms this:

   - many records have 2023 references
   - effective_at is empty
   - name/address often empty
   - organisation entity often empty

Therefore current data does not support:
=E2=80=9Cwhat is happening in Oldham right now?=E2=80=9D

FIX:
Rewrite planning collection around explicit query contracts:

collect_planning_events(
place_id,
changed_since,
application_status,
limit/cursor
)

Minimum:

   - LPA/place filter
   - real temporal filter or deterministic cursor/watermark
   - preserve source entity ID
   - preserve status and decision date
   - track source coverage/completeness
   - distinguish application submitted / validated / decided / approved /
   refused

Do not infer work demand from arbitrary historic applications.

ACCEPTANCE TEST:
For a chosen Oldham scope, every returned planning observation must:

   - resolve to Oldham (or documented catchment)
   - have a source entity/reference
   - have observed_at
   - have meaningful event/effective date OR explicitly UNKNOWN
   - be replayable from source evidence.

P0.3 =E2=80=94 demo claims are leaking into canonical opportunity output

File:

   - uk_boring/earn.py

Example:
_find_upgrades() emits:

   - =E2=80=9CEV charger demand up 31% in North West=E2=80=9D
   - =E2=80=9CCertified installers in short supply=E2=80=9D
   - training costs ~=C2=A3280
   - confidence =3D 0.8

There is no provenance attached.

This violates the system=E2=80=99s own anti-bullshit rule.

REMOVE every unsupported market_analysis opportunity immediately.

Rule:
NO Route may contain a concrete factual claim unless it has:

   - observation IDs,
   - source refs,
   - transform lineage,
   - freshness.

Conceptual/demo routes belong in fixtures only, never live results.
P0.4 =E2=80=94 expected economic value is currently fabricated

Examples in uk_boring/earn.py:

   - planning-derived work =3D =C2=A3500
   - contract value =3D 10% of total
   - flip margin =3D sold price =C3=97 30%
   - repair cost text =3D =C2=A330=E2=80=9380

These are demo heuristics presented in the same object as sourced
observations.

That is dangerous.

FIX:
Every economic number needs a METHOD.

Example:

ExpectedValue:
amount
currency
method_id
method_version
inputs[]
uncertainty_interval
truth_class

If there is no defensible estimate:
expected_value =3D UNKNOWN

Do not reward routes for invented precision.
P0.5 =E2=80=94 broad exception swallowing makes the system silently lie by =
omission

uk_boring/earn.py repeatedly does:

try:
=E2=80=A6
except Exception:
pass

For an agent-facing economic system this is unacceptable.

A broken collector/parser can make the endpoint quietly return fewer
opportunities and appear healthy.

FIX:
Use explicit typed failures:

   - SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
   - SCHEMA_CHANGED
   - NORMALIZATION_FAILED
   - STALE_DATA
   - ENTITY_AMBIGUOUS
   - SEMANTIC_UNCERTAIN

Every candidate generator returns:

GeneratorResult {
routes[]
status
errors[]
source_health[]
}

The top-level response can then say:
=E2=80=9CContracts source unavailable; results exclude public procurement.=
=E2=80=9D

Do not silently pass.
P1 =E2=80=94 ARCHITECTURAL CONVERGENCE P1.1 =E2=80=94 there are duplicate c=
anonical models

Examples:

   - core/capability_envelope.py defines CapabilityEnvelope
   - uk_boring/earn.py defines a different CapabilityEnvelope
   - core/route.py defines Route
   - uk_boring/earn.py defines Opportunity
   - core/storage.py implements storage
   - core/normalize.py implements another storage layer
   - shared/schema.py / shared/entities.py / shared/normalize.py retain
   older architecture

This is now the main codebase risk.

FIX:
One canonical package only.

TARGET:

core/
observation.py
source.py
capability_envelope.py
route.py
evidence.py
decision_spec.py
receipt.py
hypothesis.py
storage/
quality/

Everything else imports these types.

DELETE / MIGRATE:

   - local CapabilityEnvelope in uk_boring/earn.py
   - local Opportunity in uk_boring/earn.py
   - duplicate evidence types
   - duplicate normalize/storage paths
   - garden-specific shared schemas from shared/

Use core.Route as the ONLY public route representation.
P1.2 =E2=80=94 Observation IDs are not adequate for a temporal garden

Current IDs are based on identity fields such as:

   - garden
   - source
   - entity
   - metric
   - effective/event time

but not necessarily:

   - observed_at
   - value/raw content hash

If effective_at is empty (as it currently is for many planning records),
repeated observations of changed source state can collide under the same ID=
.

This breaks the time moat.

FIX:
Separate:

FactKey / SeriesKey:
=E2=80=9CWhat real-world thing/metric is this?=E2=80=9D

ObservationID:
=E2=80=9CThis exact observation event.=E2=80=9D

Recommended:

series_key =3D
hash(source_id, source_entity_id, metric)

observation_id =3D
hash(series_key, observed_at, raw_hash)

Optional state_hash =3D
hash(normalized value)

Then:

   - identical snapshots can be deduped by state_hash
   - changed state creates a new observation
   - history remains reconstructable.

Do not use one ID for both identity and observation event.
P1.3 =E2=80=94 canonical JSONL cannot be the long-term warehouse

Current repo size is already very large and canonical JSONL is committed
into Git.

That does not scale with the thesis.

Git should contain:

   - schemas
   - transforms
   - small fixtures
   - manifests/checksums
   - evals

Not:

   - years of raw observations
   - high-volume marketplace history

TARGET:

   - Postgres initially for canonical/queryable structured state
   - object storage for raw artifacts
   - append-only receipt log
   - optional analytical store later

Keep local JSONL as DEV FIXTURE backend only.

Create a storage interface now so backend can change without garden changes=
.
P1.4 =E2=80=94 source registry needs real licensing semantics

Example:
eBay source licence is described as:
=E2=80=9Ctransformative use=E2=80=9D

That is not a licence.

Each source must include:

   - legal/source owner
   - access method
   - actual licence/terms category
   - allowed retention
   - allowed redistribution
   - required attribution
   - rate constraints
   - data classification
   - review date

If unknown, mark:
LICENCE_UNKNOWN / REUSE_UNVERIFIED

Do not turn uncertainty into a permissive label.
P2 =E2=80=94 ONE CONNECTOR OUTWARD

The repo currently advertises six MCP servers and ~86 tools.

That is the previous architecture.

Externally, the user/agent should see UKGraph.

Primary high-level tools:

ukgraph.earn()
ukgraph.do()
ukgraph.value()
ukgraph.find()
ukgraph.watch()

